00:00:53.634 --> 00:00:58.067
I feel like I learned
the most I've ever learned.

00:00:58.067 --> 00:00:59.300
Like it was --
-In your entire life.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:02.701
-Yeah, totally.
I really changed as a person.

00:01:02.701 --> 00:01:05.868
And long story short, like,
I think like in the beginning

00:01:05.868 --> 00:01:10.100
was I started this album,
what was a really like

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:12.567
low mental health period for me.

00:01:12.567 --> 00:01:15.834
And I only really --
I only wanted to go back

00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:21.667
in the studio and work
if it felt like something

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:25.067
that helped me on my journey
to feeling better

00:01:25.067 --> 00:01:28.667
and was a source of joy
and healing and fun.

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:29.868
And I did it completely
different

00:01:29.868 --> 00:01:31.567
than I've ever written
any other one before.

00:01:31.567 --> 00:01:33.868
I was a really,
really small group of people.

00:01:33.868 --> 00:01:36.067
It started with me
and my friend Scott

00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:39.901
in like my home, like house,
bedroom in Miami.

00:01:39.901 --> 00:01:41.033
-Just working on stuff.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:43.767
-Just like talking
about anxiety, basically.

00:01:43.767 --> 00:01:45.634
-Yeah.
-I think the difference between

00:01:45.634 --> 00:01:48.601
me now and me before
was I think in the --

00:01:48.601 --> 00:01:51.400
in the writing process,
sometimes I just felt like

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:53.167
I had a lot to prove.

00:01:53.167 --> 00:01:54.567
Like I was just like,
I want people, you know,

00:01:54.567 --> 00:01:56.801
I want this person to think
I'm a good songwriter,

00:01:56.801 --> 00:01:58.000
I want whatever, whatever.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.634
And also I think my own battles

00:02:00.634 --> 00:02:03.467
with like with anxiety
and mental health stuff.

00:02:03.467 --> 00:02:05.734
I was young
and I felt a lot of shame

00:02:05.734 --> 00:02:07.534
in talking about it,
I felt like I had to go

00:02:07.534 --> 00:02:09.467
and just like have it
all together

00:02:09.467 --> 00:02:12.434
and be this kind of, like,
confident, you know,

00:02:12.434 --> 00:02:14.234
"pop star" that just --

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:16.801
And on the inside,
I was just like,

00:02:16.801 --> 00:02:18.133
you know,
like really struggling.

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:19.868
And this time around,
I was like, you know what?

00:02:19.868 --> 00:02:21.267
I'm not trying to prove
anything to anybody.

00:02:21.267 --> 00:02:22.901
I'm not trying
to impress anybody.

00:02:22.901 --> 00:02:28.334
I'm just trying to be me,
be vulnerable,

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:30.801
make songs
that are really just like,

00:02:30.801 --> 00:02:32.701
just be [bleep] honest.

00:02:32.701 --> 00:02:33.734
Sorry for swearing.

00:02:33.734 --> 00:02:36.033
-Yeah, go for it.
I know.

00:02:36.033 --> 00:02:37.234
I love it, you know?

00:02:37.234 --> 00:02:38.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:40.434
That's exactly what we want.
-Yeah.

00:02:40.434 --> 00:02:43.567
And -- and I think
in doing that,

00:02:43.567 --> 00:02:44.767
I really -- there's like --

00:02:44.767 --> 00:02:46.234
I said this on my album
thank you's.

00:02:46.234 --> 00:02:48.267
I was like, you know,
before I felt like

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:51.467
I needed to be kind of healed
or perfect to be seen,

00:02:51.467 --> 00:02:54.534
and I realized that being seen
is what kind of

00:02:54.534 --> 00:02:55.601
is the healing thing, you know?

00:02:55.601 --> 00:02:56.934
-Yeah.

00:02:56.934 --> 00:02:59.567
-And so that's why
it's called "Familia."

00:02:59.567 --> 00:03:01.467
I started by saying
long story short.

00:03:01.467 --> 00:03:03.734
It's actually long story long.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:03.734 --> 00:03:05.667
It's actually, no,
it's a great story.

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:10.033
But I also -- I mean, there are
some good criers on here,

00:03:10.033 --> 00:03:12.467
but it's a lot of dance on here.

00:03:12.467 --> 00:03:14.000
-Totally.
-You're making people have fun.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.400
I mean, this is --
this is a journey.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.133
This is like -- it's everything.

00:03:17.133 --> 00:03:20.501
-For me, also why I name
the album "Familia,"

00:03:20.501 --> 00:03:22.601
for me, it was like
that support group

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:26.767
that I made, my collaborators,
my friends, my family,

00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:30.834
my therapist, like whatever,
like opening up to people.

00:03:30.834 --> 00:03:33.901
That kind of interdependence
and like leaning on other people

00:03:33.901 --> 00:03:37.000
is something that has
been a big,

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:39.968
has been defining,
like, word for this chapter

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:41.634
is like interdependence,
you know?

00:03:41.634 --> 00:03:43.767
